## Summary

**Ticket:** espectacular-o77 (claimed, not closed — lead closes)

**RED** (`e8b2d24`): `changed_files_from_git` signature changed to `anyhow::Result<Vec<String>>` + new unit test `changed_files_git_failure_is_explicit_error` asserting a git failure surfaces as an explicit error. Fails pre-migration with `got Ok([])`, as required.

**GREEN** (`1220eff`):
- `src/main.rs` — the raw `std::process::Command::new("git") diff --name-only HEAD` is gone; `changed_files_from_git` now delegates to `genesis::git::changed_files(root)`, which carries the documented semantics from the spec (tracked changes vs HEAD, untracked excluded while HEAD resolves, unborn-HEAD fallback). No local git logic remains, and the explicit root (cwd-derived `std::env::current_dir()` at the call site) is passed through — no cwd reliance inside the op.
- Contract decision: genesis 0.13 has **no `changed_files_lossy`** (only `uncommitted_files_lossy`), so per the brief's explicit alternative I mapped errors — the silent empty-`Vec` degradation is gone by design; git failures now propagate as anyhow errors with context from `GitError`'s Display.
- `Cargo.toml`: `genesis-vibes = "0.13"` → resolves 0.13.0.
- `tests/check_cli.rs`: fixtures become real git repos (shared `git_commit_all` helper, clean initial commit) so `--run-tests` fixtures keep pre-migration run-all selection semantics — a dirty or absent repo now activates the explicit error or test selection, both intended post-migration behaviors.

